# Rails' macro shape: a `ClassMethods` method (or any method a class body
# calls on itself) whose body `class_eval`s a string or runs `define_method`
# makes the methods on the calling class. Written in an instance method,
# nothing was marked, and `Widget#helper_made` was "no such method", exit 1,
# with `--def` blaming a gem. The class whose body calls the macro, where its
# class side reaches it, is marked; one that only includes the module is not.
# A name defined nowhere that the call's own file may make says so.
